-- #1648 — NOT GRADED BY THIS GATE. Row A of the issue's table: the body ignores the dict
-- AND the value. It has the SAME arity skew as main.mdk (`define …(i64 %arg0)` against a
-- 2-argument call), but nothing reads the mis-bound parameter, so the binary happens to
-- print the right answer: `22`, exit 0.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS IS WHY IT IS NOT THE PIN. It passes today, so an assertion on it could not
-- fail, and a fixture that cannot fail pins nothing. It is kept here because it is the
-- dangerous cell, not the harmless one: a fix validated against this shape alone would
-- look correct while leaving the skew in place. Any fix for #1648 should also be checked
-- against this file's emitted IR, not just its exit code.
--
-- Measured first-hand alongside main.mdk: check 0, run `22`, build 0, binary exit 0
-- printing `22`.
data Box a = Box Int

interface Same a where
  bar : a -> Int

impl Same (Box a) requires Eq a where
  bar _ = 22

main = println (bar (Box 7))
